      ],
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "widgets_values": [
        "HUD BOXES (multi) \u2013 how to use\n\n1. HUD Multi Detect \u2192 'objects': words to box, separated by commas or new lines (e.g. person, car, dog). Each word is one extra pass over the video, so 3 words \u2248 3x the time.\n2. HUD Render Boxes:\n   palette: neon / military / cyberpunk / thermal / mono white / mono red / pastel, or 'custom' + your own hex list in custom_palette (#FF0000, #00FF00, ...). Colours go to words in order.\n   color_by: word (one colour per word) or each box.\n   style: corners (HUD brackets), box, or both.\n   fill_opacity > 0 adds a tint inside boxes. show_score adds confidence %.\n   hold_between_frames keeps boxes steady on frames skipped by frame_stride.\n3. TimeSlice is bypassed (purple): Ctrl+B to enable.\n4. Output: ComfyUI-Shared/output/video/hud_multi_*.mp4"
      ],
      "mode": 0,
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      }
